<p id="mwCA"><b id="mwCQ">Yakov Kuzyakov</b> is a soil scientist<sup about="#mwt11" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ndiaeducationdiary_1-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ndiaeducationdiary"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ndiaeducationdiary-1"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-ndiaeducationdiary-1" id="mwCg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwCw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDA">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwDQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt14" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-staff_list_2-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"staff list"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-staff_list-2"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-staff_list-2" id="mwDg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwDw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEA">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwEQ">]</span></span></a></sup> who works at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./University_of_Göttingen" title="University of Göttingen" id="mwEg">University of Göttingen</a> at the Soil Science of Temperate Ecosystems department.<sup about="#mwt15" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-staff_list_2-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"staff list"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-staff_list-2" id="mwEw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwFA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwFg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt18" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-3"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-3" id="mwFw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwGA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGQ">[</span>3<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwGg">]</span></span></a></sup> He is also affiliated with the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Patrice_Lumumba_Peoples'_Friendship_University_of_Russia" title="Patrice Lumumba Peoples' Friendship University of Russia" id="mwGw">RUDN University</a>.<sup about="#mwt21" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-4" id="mwHA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwHQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHg">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwHw">]</span></span></a></sup> Since September 2026 his work has been scrutinized, so far five of his papers have been retracted due to serious ethical violations during the peer review and editorial process.<sup about="#mwt24" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Liang_5-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Liang"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Liang-5"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Liang-5" id="mwIA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwIQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwIw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt27" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Maharjan_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Maharjan"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Maharjan-6"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Maharjan-6" id="mwJA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwJQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJg">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwJw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt30" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Qiu_7-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Qiu"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Qiu-7"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Qiu-7" id="mwKA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwKQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwKw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt33" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Qiu2_8-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Qiu2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Qiu2-8"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Qiu2-8" id="mwLA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLg">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwLw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt36" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wu_9-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wu"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Wu-9"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Wu-9" id="mwMA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwMQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMg">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}' id="mwNA"/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwNQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Research_and_career">Research and career</h2>
<p id="mwNg">He was a professor at the department of Agroecosystem Research at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./University_of_Bayreuth" title="University of Bayreuth" id="mwNw">University of Bayreuth</a> until 2011.<sup about="#mwt39" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-10"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-10" id="mwOA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwOQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOg">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwOw">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2011, he has headed the department of Soil Science of Temperate Ecosystems and the department of Agricultural Soil Science at the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./University_of_Göttingen" title="University of Göttingen" id="mwPA">University of Göttingen</a>.<sup about="#mwt40" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-staff_list_2-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"staff list"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-staff_list-2" id="mwPQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPw">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt43" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-11" id="mwQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQw">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwRA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwRQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Controversies">Controversies</h2>
<p id="mwRg">In 2026, his work came under scrutiny for unethical behavior. As an editor for the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Elsevier" title="Elsevier" id="mwRw">Elsevier</a> European Journal of Soil Biology, he edited several of his own papers. As of September 2026, four of the papers in that journal that he authored and edited himself were retracted. Aside from editing four of his own papers,<sup about="#mwt44" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Liang_5-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Liang"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Liang-5" id="mwSA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSg">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt45" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Maharjan_6-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Maharjan"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Maharjan-6" id="mwTA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTg">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt46" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Qiu_7-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Qiu"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Qiu-7" id="mwUA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt47" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Qiu2_8-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Qiu2"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Qiu2-8" id="mwVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVg">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">]</span></span></a></sup> three papers had also been reviewed by at least one reviewer closely linked to him, compromising the editorial process.<sup about="#mwt50" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-12" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-12"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-12" id="mwWA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwWQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWg">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt51" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Maharjan_6-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Maharjan"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Maharjan-6" id="mwXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXg">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt52" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Qiu_7-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Qiu"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Qiu-7" id="mwYA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYg">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt53" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Qiu2_8-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Qiu2"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Qiu2-8" id="mwZA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZg">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZw">]</span></span></a></sup> A fifth paper he authored in a second Elsevier journal, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Science_of_the_Total_Environment" title="Science of the Total Environment" id="mwaA">Science of the Total Environment</a>, was retracted due to suspicious changes in authors on the paper during the review process.<sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wu_9-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wu"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-Wu-9" id="mwaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaw">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwbQ"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Scientific_achievements">Scientific achievements</h2>
<p id="mwbg">Yakov is one of the most cited scientists in the world and has published more than a thousand scientific papers throughout his career.<sup about="#mwt55" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ndiaeducationdiary_1-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ndiaeducationdiary"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-ndiaeducationdiary-1" id="mwbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcQ">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt58" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-13"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-13" id="mwcw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdQ">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdg">]</span></span></a></sup> He has been a world's top 2% ranked scientists for 7 years straight since 2020.<sup about="#mwt61" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-14" id="mwdw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mweA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mweQ">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mweg">]</span></span></a></sup> He was a highly cited researcher in the field of Agricultural Sciences between 2015 and 2020,<sup about="#mwt64" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-15"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-15" id="mwew"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfQ">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfg">]</span></span></a></sup> and was included in the list of the most cited Russian scientists in 2017.<sup about="#mwt67" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-16"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-16" id="mwfw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgQ">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgg">]</span></span></a></sup> Four of his papers published in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Soil_Biology_and_Biochemistry" title="Soil Biology and Biochemistry" id="mwgw">Soil Biology and Biochemistry</a> have been listed as the most cited over the last 50 years.<sup about="#mwt70" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-17" id="mwhA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhg">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwiA"><h2 data-mw-wikitext="" id="Research_interests">Research interests</h2>
<p id="mwiQ">Kuzyakov specialises in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Soil_ecology" title="Soil ecology" id="mwig">soil ecology</a> and soil <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Biogeochemistry" title="Biogeochemistry" id="mwiw">biogeochemistry</a> (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Lipids" title="Lipids" class="mw-redirect" id="mwjA">lipids</a>, low molecular organic substances), <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Agriculture" title="Agriculture" id="mwjQ">agriculture</a>, land use, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Agroecology" title="Agroecology" id="mwjg">agroecology</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Carbon_cycle" title="Carbon cycle" id="mwjw">C</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Nitrogen_cycle" title="Nitrogen cycle" id="mwkA">N cycles</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Priming_(microbiology)" title="Priming (microbiology)" id="mwkQ">priming effects</a>, soil-plant interactions (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="./Rhizosphere" title="Rhizosphere" id="mwkg">rhizosphere</a> processes), in-depth study of rhizodeposition, partitioning of CO<sub id="mwkw">2</sub> fluxes from soil and application of radioactive and stable isotope labelling approaches in soil science.<sup about="#mwt71" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-staff_list_2-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"staff list"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-staff_list-2" id="mwlA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlg">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt72" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ndiaeducationdiary_1-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ndiaeducationdiary"}}'><a href="./Yakov_Kuzyakov#cite_note-ndiaeducationdiary-1" id="mwmA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwmQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmg">[</span>1<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

